>
  <section id="product" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Product</h2>
    <p>
      CADCAMFUN v6 is a native desktop application: 2D drawing, a 3D viewport, toolpath generation,
      G-code export, a materials / tools / machine library, cost estimates, an AI assistant, a plugin
      host, and auto-update. It is local-first and works offline. The window is Tauri v2. Application
      logic runs in a Bun sidecar. Geometry and CAM live in <code>packages/core</code> and do not
      open a database or a socket.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read these three files before changing code. They are the record this site follows.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Question</th><th>File</th><th>What it decides</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>What is in scope, and who owns which directory?</td>
          <td><code>specs/00-overview.md</code></td>
          <td>Goal, stack, task board WP0–WP14, definition of done.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>How is Effect, SQLite, and a module written?</td>
          <td><code>specs/01-conventions.md</code></td>
          <td>Effect v4 shape, database rules, units, agent workflow.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>What is the next implementation step?</td>
          <td><code>specs/roadmap/README.md</code></td>
          <td>Order RM-00–RM-11. The current step is RM-01.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout title="Contracts and sequence">
      <p>
        Design specs (<code>specs/00</code> through <code>specs/28</code>, plus <code>specs/ai/</code>)
        own contracts. <code>specs/roadmap/</code> owns sequence. When a paragraph on this site and a
        spec disagree, follow the spec. When the roadmap is cited, follow
        <code>specs/roadmap/README.md</code> and <code>specs/roadmap/00-how-to-follow.md</code> for
        order. Do not use <code>specs/20-integral-roadmap.md</code> or
        <code>specs/21-integration-master-plan.md</code> as the work queue.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
    <p>
      <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> §6 requires HTTP parity with all 195 legacy route files listed
      in <code>specs/api-inventory.md</code>, and a SolidJS UI that matches the legacy app. That
      parity is still open: WP3, WP4, WP6, and WP7 are <code>in progress</code> on the task board.
      Cloud services (Stripe, email, OAuth) stay behind an Effect service with a local default. The
      HTTP contract stays the same. v6.0 local identity is one <code>User</code> row. There is no
      login screen in that local profile.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="stack" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <p>
      Pins below are the ones in <code>README.md</code>, <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> §1, and
      the workspace <code>package.json</code> files. The layout table in
      <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> §3 still says “Vite + React” for <code>apps/desktop</code>.
      The stack table in §1, the README, and <code>apps/desktop/package.json</code>
      (<code>solid-js</code>, <code>vite-plugin-solid</code>) are SolidJS. Build and edit the UI as
      SolidJS.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Concern</th><th>Choice</th><th>Where it is pinned</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Runtime, package manager, tests</td>
          <td>Bun</td>
          <td>Root <code>packageManager</code> is <code>bun@1.4.2</code>. Tests are <code>bun:test</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Application logic</td>
          <td>Effect <code>4.0.0-rc.112</code></td>
          <td>Every package that depends on <code>effect</code>. Required by <code>@nikcli-ai/sdk-next</code>. One copy, so <code>Context</code> tags match.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Persistence</td>
          <td>Drizzle <code>1.0.0-beta.22</code> + SQLite (<code>bun:sqlite</code>)</td>
          <td><code>packages/db</code>. <code>drizzle-kit</code> is the same beta.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Desktop shell</td>
          <td>Tauri v2</td>
          <td><code>apps/desktop/src-tauri</code>. CLI is <code>@tauri-apps/cli</code> in the desktop devDependencies. Rust 1.96 is the toolchain named in the overview. Do not <code>cargo install</code> the Tauri CLI.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>UI</td>
          <td>SolidJS + Vite + TypeScript, Three.js viewport</td>
          <td><code>apps/desktop</code>. <code>solid-js</code> ^1.9, <code>three</code> ^0.180, Vite 7, Tailwind v3.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>AI</td>
          <td>nikcli host (<code>@nikcli-ai/sdk-next</code>) and AI SDK v7 (<code>ai</code>)</td>
          <td><code>packages/ai</code>. Direct calls use <code>@ai-sdk/*</code>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Effect’s version-matched docs are on disk at
      <code>packages/db/node_modules/effect/ai-docs/src/</code> (Bun does not hoist; any workspace
      <code>node_modules/effect/ai-docs/src/</code> is the same pin). Read the folder for the API you
      are calling. Do not write Effect v3 from memory, and do not bump <code>effect</code> in a
      single package. Root <code>overrides</code> also pin
      <code>@effect/platform-node</code> and <code>@effect/platform-node-shared</code> to
      <code>4.0.0-rc.112</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

