      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Source map" eyebrow="Paths" href="/docs/source-map">
        <p>Directories for CAD, CAM, HTTP, the window, and the specs.</p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="commands" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Commands</h2>
    <p>
      Run these from the repository root. The root <code>test</code> script is wider than the
      README line: <code>bun run test</code> executes <code>bun test packages apps scripts</code>.
      The README command stops at packages and apps.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash" title="Repo root">
{`bun install
bun test packages apps
bunx tsc -p packages/core/tsconfig.json
bun run db:generate
bun run db:migrate
bun run desktop:dev
bun run build
bun run build:sidecar
bun run build:desktop`}
    </DocCode>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Script</th><th>Root package.json</th><th>What you get</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>db:generate</code></td>
          <td><code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/db generate</code></td>
          <td><code>drizzle-kit generate</code> from <code>packages/db/src/schema.ts</code> into <code>packages/db/drizzle/</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>db:migrate</code></td>
          <td><code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/db migrate</code></td>
          <td><code>bun src/migrate.ts</code>. Default file string is <code>./data/cadcamfun.db</code>. See <a href="/docs/guides/quickstart">Quickstart</a> for which directory that is relative to.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>desktop:dev</code></td>
          <td><code>bun run build:sidecar &amp;&amp; bun run --filter @cadcamfun/desktop tauri dev</code></td>
          <td>Compiles the real sidecar, copies migrations, then opens the Tauri dev window. Vite is <code>http://localhost:1420</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>build:sidecar</code></td>
          <td><code>bun scripts/build.ts --only=compile,resources</code></td>
          <td>Sidecar binary plus <code>packages/db/drizzle</code> copied to <code>apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/migrations/</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>build:desktop</code></td>
          <td><code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/desktop build</code></td>
          <td>Vite build of the webview only. It does not run <code>tauri build</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>build</code></td>
          <td><code>bun scripts/build.ts</code></td>
          <td>Full pipeline in <code>scripts/build.ts</code>: install, typecheck, compile, resources, bundle, artifacts.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>typecheck</code></td>
          <td><code>turbo run typecheck &amp;&amp; tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit</code></td>
          <td>Every package <code>typecheck</code> script, then the root project.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>generate</code></td>
          <td><code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/api generate</code></td>
          <td>Regenerate HTTP clients into <code>packages/api/src/sdk</code> and <code>packages/api/src/client</code>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="boundaries" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <p>
      Dependency direction, from the README, with no cycles:
      <code>core</code> ← <code>api</code> ← sidecar;
      <code>db</code> ← sidecar;
      <code>ai</code> and <code>plugin-sdk</code> ← sidecar.
      The desktop imports API types only. <code>core</code> and <code>api</code> must not import
      <code>db</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>apps/desktop/package.json</code> also depends on <code>@cadcamfun/core</code>, and
      <code>apps/desktop/src</code> imports it from the viewport and the CAD/CAM features (geometry,
      toolpaths, sketches). <code>apps/mobile/package.json</code> depends on
      <code>@cadcamfun/api</code> only. Do not add <code>@cadcamfun/db</code> to
      <code>packages/core</code>, <code>packages/api</code>, <code>apps/desktop</code>, or
      <code>apps/mobile</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Internal units are millimetres and radians. Convert to degrees only at the UI or G-code
      boundary. G-code numbers use a fixed decimal count (default 3). Do not format them with
      implicit <code>toString</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>.reference/</code> is the previous Next.js, Prisma, and Stripe/Better Auth tree. It is
      git-ignored and read-only. Use it as domain knowledge. Do not import it, and do not copy a
      module in verbatim: <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> says several legacy modules contain bugs
      (see <code>specs/04-core-cam.md</code>).
    </p>
    <DocCallout title="Leave .env files closed" type="warn">
      <p>
        Do not read, print, or copy values from <code>.env*</code> files. They are legacy and unused.
        The sidecar reads configuration once, in <code>apps/sidecar/src/config.ts</code>, through
        Effect <code>Config</code>. The shell passes <code>CADCAMFUN_TOKEN</code>,
        <code>CADCAMFUN_DATA_DIR</code>, and <code>CADCAMFUN_MIGRATIONS_DIR</code> when it spawns the
        binary. Do not invent a dotenv loader in another package.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="next" class="doc-section">
    <h2>What to do next</h2>
    <p>
      The current roadmap step is the first row whose status is <code>in progress</code>, otherwise
      the first <code>pending</code> row. That row is <strong>RM-01</strong>,
      <code>specs/roadmap/01-action-catalogue.md</code>. Its owners, as written on the roadmap, are
      WP8 <code>packages/ai</code>, WP4 AI handler adapters, WP3 shared action schemas, and WP6 AI
      tool consumers (scopes are in the step spec).
    </p>
    <p>
      RM-11 is also marked <code>in progress</code> (HTTP face + plugin built). It is not the
      current step. It depends on RM-01 and RM-03. Do not start it as the next task because the
      status cell contains “in progress”.
    </p>
    <p>
      An agent edits only the directories that step owns. A contract change is an edit to the design
      spec first, with a change-log line, and then the code. Do not commit unless asked. Code,
      comments, docs, and commit messages are English.
    </p>
  </section>
